"/athletes/146399"} "Tatjana Schoenmaker-Smith"] " was the defending gold medalist and, three days before this final, she had added a gold in the 100 backstroke. Her biggest challengers were American " [:a {:href "/athletes/2506216"} "Kate Douglass"] " and Dutchwoman " [:a {:href "/athletes/145518"} "Tes Schouten"] ", who between them had swum 2:19 or better seven times in 2024."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The three qualified 1-2-3 in the semi-finals, led by Douglass, with Schoenmaker-Smith in second. They would match that finish in the final. Douglass won gold by taking the lead on the second lap and holding it the rest of the way, although Schoenmaker-Smith was never far behind, finishing only 36/100ths in arrears. Schouten took the bronze, although she was never really in the race for gold-silver. For the recently married Schoenmaker-Smith, it was the final race of her competitive career, as she announced her retirement after the race. She finished her career with four medals in Olympic breaststroke events, two golds and two silvers."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/2506216"} "Kate Douglass"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "2:23.44 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "2:19.74 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "2:19.24 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/146399"} "Tatjana Schoenmaker-Smith"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RSA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/RSA.png"}] "RSA"]] [:td {} "2:21.57 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "2:19.94 (2 h2)"] [:td {} 